  "question": {
    "text": "A ray of laser of a wavelength <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>630</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>nm</mi></math> is incident at an angle of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>30</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math> at the diamond-air interface. It is going from diamond to air. The refractive index of diamond is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>42</mn></math> and that of air is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math>. Choose the correct option.",
    "image": null
  },
